touch/ — per-device touch-driver harvest (LOCAL ONLY, gitignored).

Layout (single level — no double `touch/touch`):

  touch/<device>/<maj.min>/<patch>/android<XX>/<4k|16k>/
    <mod>_android<XX>-<maj.min>.<patch>_<4k|16k>.ko

Example:

  touch/shiba/6.1/157/android14/4k/goodix_brl_touch_android14-6.1.157_4k.ko

Flow (see fox_build_callback.sh build_device_touch_cpios):
- The harvest lives HERE, in the source tree (put there by hand from
  tools/unpack_modules or tools/extract_touch_modules.py --out).
- At build time (--second-call, BEFORE the LGZ pack and manifest
  generation) the callback packs installer/modules/<device>.lgz
  (root-relative system/lib64/modules/touch/... paths) straight from
  the recovery ramdisk copy ($TARGET_DIR/.../touch/<device>), then
  deletes the packed files from the ramdisk (directories stay) so
  they never enter the cluster, the snapshot manifest, the file
  lists, or the image.
- At install time the matching lgz is pushed INTO the recovery
  payload (--inject-lgz); at boot the touch-unpack stage extracts
  /<device>.lgz to /.

Rules:
- One directory per device, any kernel snapshots inside (5.10/5.15/
  6.1/6.6 — the loader scores the closest, cross-loads inside 6.1.x).
- <pagesize> is 4k or 16k and is a HARD filter (never cross-loads).
- NEVER commit harvested .ko files (see .gitignore): only this
  README is tracked.
